        "title": "fix(openai): bound realtime voice websocket payload at 16 MiB",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe ws library defaults to 100 MiB maxPayload. The OpenAI realtime voice\nprovider creates a WebSocket connection without an explicit limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd maxPayload: OPENAI_VOICE_WS_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES (16 MiB) to the WebSocket\nconstructor, consistent with the shared bounded-resource cap used across other\nprovider/client fixes on main.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe ws library enforces maxPayload internally. Real behavior proof shows\noversized frames are rejected with close code 1009.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
